<title>FRANCE: Breakdown of French ports hit by one-day strike.</title>
<headline>Breakdown of French ports hit by one-day strike.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>A spokeswoman for French port association UNIM gave the following list of ports hit by a one-day dockers' strike on Monday.</p>
<p>Union confirmation was not available.</p>
<p>PORTS AFFECTED BY STRIKE</p>
<p>Bordeaux, Boulogne, Calais, Le Havre, Cherbourg, Lorient, Nantes, La Rochelle, Sete, Marseille.</p>
<p>PORTS PARTIALLY AFFECTED</p>
<p>Rouen (one hour), Port-La Nouvelle, Bayonne (strike call not obeyed, according to employers).</p>
<p>PORTS NOT AFFECTED</p>
<p>Brest (earlier reported on strike), Caen, Dunkirk, Fecamp, Port-Vendres, Saint-Malo, Saint-Nazaire.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
